    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given a list of non-negative integers, arrange them so that, written one after another, they form the **largest possible number**. Return it as a string (it may be too big for any integer type)."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/c766bc79-4dc9-4f4d-b0d3-168f3caaa2a3.svg",
      "alt": "Comparing 3 and 30: 3 then 30 gives 330, 30 then 3 gives 303, so 3 goes first. Sorting 3, 30, 34, 5, 9 with that rule gives 9, 5, 34, 3, 30, which joins into 9534330.",
