    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**All zeros** — `[0, 0]` gives `\"0\"`.",
        "**Prefixes** — `3` vs `30` vs `34`: the comparator handles them; plain string sorting puts 30 before 34 but gets 3 vs 30 wrong.",
        "**A single number** — returned as a string.",
        "**Equal concatenations** — `12` and `1212` compare equal; either order is fine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Smallest number** — the same comparator reversed, with care about leading zeros.",
        "**Form the largest number from digits with constraints** — greedy choices over sorted digits.",
        "**Relative Sort Array** — another order defined by a comparator. Two lessons back."
      ]
    }
  ],
